										class="kt-row-column-wrap kt-has-2-columns kt-gutter-default kt-v-gutter-default kt-row-valign-top kt-row-layout-equal kt-tab-layout-inherit kt-m-colapse-left-to-right kt-mobile-layout-row">
										<div class="wp-block-kadence-column inner-column-1 kadence-column_567847-86">
											<div class="kt-inside-inner-col">
												<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy"
														decoding="async" width="1017" height="774"
														src="./Jurassic Days_ Dino Statue Driving Tour_files/Amazing-Hands.jpeg"
														alt="Amazing Hands Dinosaur Statue" class="wp-image-14155"
														srcset="https://carnegiemnh.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Amazing-Hands.jpeg 1017w, https://carnegiemnh.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Amazing-Hands-300x228.jpeg 300w, https://carnegiemnh.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Amazing-Hands-768x584.jpeg 768w"
														sizes="auto, (max-width: 1017px) 100vw, 1017px"></figure>
											</div>
										</div>



										<div class="wp-block-kadence-column inner-column-2 kadence-column_54ef1b-4a">
											<div class="kt-inside-inner-col">
												<p><strong>Eighth Stop:</strong> Amazing
													Hands<br><strong>Coordinates:</strong> 40.442526, -79.919394</p>



												<p>An awesome garden-inspired dinosaur created by children at the
													Children’s Institute lives at the Squirrel Hill location.&nbsp; Wave
													hello to this dinosaur from across the parking lot off of
													Northumberland Street.</p>



												<div class="wp-block-image">
													<figure class="aligncenter size-large"><a
															href="http://www.amazingkids.org/"><img loading="lazy"
																decoding="async" width="320" height="80"
																src="./Jurassic Days_ Dino Statue Driving Tour_files/logo2.png"
																alt="The Children&#39;s Institute"
																class="wp-image-14157"
																srcset="https://carnegiemnh.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/logo2.png 320w, https://carnegiemnh.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/logo2-300x75.png 300w"
																sizes="auto, (max-width: 320px) 100vw, 320px"></a>
													</figure>
												</div>
											</div>
										</div>
									</div>
								</div>
							</div>



							<div class="wp-block-kadence-rowlayout alignnone">
								<div id="kt-layout-id_3f2ff8-2f" class="kt-row-layout-inner kt-layout-id_3f2ff8-2f">
									<div
										class="kt-row-column-wrap kt-has-2-columns kt-gutter-default kt-v-gutter-default kt-row-valign-top kt-row-layout-equal kt-tab-layout-inherit kt-m-colapse-left-to-right kt-mobile-layout-row">
										<div class="wp-block-kadence-column inner-column-1 kadence-column_10eeeb-e8">
											<div class="kt-inside-inner-col">
												<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img loading="lazy"
														decoding="async" width="768" height="1024"
														src="./Jurassic Days_ Dino Statue Driving Tour_files/Spectrasaurus.jpeg"
														alt="Spectrasaurus" class="wp-image-14158"
														srcset="https://carnegiemnh.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Spectrasaurus.jpeg 768w, https://carnegiemnh.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/Spectrasaurus-225x300.jpeg 225w"
														sizes="auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px"></figure>
											</div>
										</div>



										<div class="wp-block-kadence-column inner-column-2 kadence-column_6f2852-c2">
											<div class="kt-inside-inner-col">
												<p><strong>Ninth Stop:</strong>
													Spectrasaurus<br><strong>Coordinates:</strong> 40.450149, -79.945179
												</p>



												<p>This dinosaur is located on private property at the corner of
													Ellsworth and Devonshire in Squirrel Hill.&nbsp; Easily visible from
													the sidewalk, this colorful dinosaur was designed to mimic the
													bright warning colors of poisonous tree frogs.</p>
											</div>
										</div>
									</div>
								</div>
							</div>



							<div class="wp-block-kadence-rowlayout alignnone">
